# nr-tui-pickers-extensions: integration fragment

Fills `native/core/crates/mixdog-tui/src/pickers/extensions.rs` and `src/pickers/extensions/` (the MCP, Skills, Plugins, Memory,
Project and Resume pickers, the MCP sign-in flow, the double-Esc message selector and the disabled-skill set). Nothing in it
was compiled by its author (no cargo in the task); the lead compiles it with the wave.

## Hot files

None. The crate is already a workspace member and takes no new dependency edge: the code uses `mixdog-js`, `mixdog-term`
(`os::{FolderPick, FolderPickOptions}`), `mixdog-tui-style`, `mixdog-tui-widgets` (`picker`), `serde_json`, all in the crate's
`Cargo.toml` already. No protocol row, no `SERVICE_PENDING` name: every store method it calls (`mcpStatus`,
`setMcpServerEnabled`, `skillsStatus`, `pluginsStatus`, `updatePlugin`, `enablePluginMcp`, `removePlugin`, `memoryControl`,
`listProjects`, `addProject`, `setCwd`, `listSessions`, `resume`, `rewindToItem`, `getDisabledSkills`, `setDisabledSkills`,
`beginMcpOAuthLogin`, `getMcpOAuthLoginStatus`, `completeMcpOAuthLogin`, `cancelMcpOAuthLogin`, `signOutMcpServer`) is the
store method the Node code called, through `AppCtx::store_call`.

## What the wiring (nr-tui-app-run) must apply

* Implement `pickers::extensions::ExtensionsHost` (a supertrait over `app::AppCtx`) on the object that owns the application
  state; every method has a doc line naming the Node symbol. The panel surface it needs is the one `surface::owner::PanelSurface`
  already is: `paint(claim, panel)` is `own.paint(panel)` (a guarded write that re-arms the claim, `None` clears and keeps the
  flow), `close_claim` is `own.close()` (ownership is gone for good), `clear_context` is `own.context(null)` (supersedes, claim
  re-armed). `SurfaceClaim.epoch` is the token. The picker panel type of the surface wraps `ExtPanel` (it implements
  `PanelValue` and `IndexModePanel`); the shell layout's `PickerLayout.kind` (Node's `picker?.kind === 'project'`, which keeps
  the banner and the height reserved) is `ExtPanel::layout_kind`, not `ExtPanel::kind` (`_kind`, the panel identity: the
  folder-dialog overlay has a layout kind `project` and no `_kind`); `ExtPanel::to_props(columns)` is its `PickerProps`, `ExtPanel::adjustable()` is whether
  Left/Right toggle, `ExtPanel::items[..].marker_tone` maps to `theme.success` / `theme.inactive`.
* Keys on a painted `ExtPanel` go to `Extensions::select(host, panel, row)` (Enter), `adjust` (Left/Right: the MCP and Skills
  toggles), `key` (a character key: `c` and `r` of the project list) and `cancel` (Esc). One `Extensions` lives for the life of
  the application: it holds the MCP toggle settle guard, the Memory picker's Esc target, the project list request counter and the
  MCP sign-in.
* `SlashHost::open(opener, options)` calls `Extensions::open(host, opener, &options)` for the openers `Extensions::serves`
  names (Mcp, McpServers, Skills, ProjectSkills, Plugins, MemoryCore, Project, Resume); it answers `None` for any other.
  Options: `{ "initialEntry": true }` for Project; for MemoryCore `{ "returnTo": "<opener name>" }` (the Settings row passes
  `"settings"`; Node passed a function), `{ "returnTo": null }` for the standalone `/memory`, no key to inherit the earlier
  target. The settings task (nr-tui-pickers-settings) opens Memory that way.
* `SlashHost::login_mcp_server`, `logout_mcp_server`, `register_project`, `enter_project` are `Extensions.login.login`,
  `.logout`, `Extensions::register_project` and `Extensions::enter_project(host, path, notice, register)` (the slash `/project`
  argument path uses `notice: true, register: true`).
* MCP sign-in prompt: `login` shows the shared `oauth-code` provider prompt with the field `mcpFlowId`
  (`mcp_login::is_login_prompt`). For such a prompt the shared prompt handler's callbacks are: `oauth_complete_code` ->
  `Extensions.login.complete_code(host, code)`; `oauth_failure_return` -> `Extensions.login.failure_return(host)`;
  `oauth_success_return` -> true (no further picker); dismissing the prompt -> `Extensions.login.cancel(host)`. The poll timer:
  while `Extensions.login.poll_due_at()` is `Some(t)`, call `Extensions.login.poll(host)` once `now_ms >= t` (the flow asks again
  every `mcp_login::POLL_MS`).
* First screen: when the session is empty and onboarding does not own the screen, paint `project::initial_project_panel(cwd)`
  and run `Extensions::open_project(host, true)` while `ExtPanel::initial_pending` is set (App.jsx `_projectInitialPending`).
* Double Esc on an empty idle prompt: `message_selector::has_user_messages(items)` decides whether the Esc counts,
  `message_selector::open_message_selector(host)` opens the list (it shows its own hint when there is nothing to jump to). The
  prompt callbacks it needs are `ExtensionsHost::{show_prompt_hint, clear_prompt_hint, sync_prompt_layout_rows,
  set_prompt_draft_override, install_pasted_images, install_pasted_texts}` (`set_prompt_draft_override`'s id is a clock value).
* At start: `disabled_skills::load_disabled_skills(host)` (the set is read once; a failed probe leaves every skill enabled).
* `ExtensionsHost::pick_folder` is `mixdog_term::os::pick_folder(options)` (blocking while the dialog is open: run the opener from
  the task that owns the result); `copy_to_clipboard` is the terminal clipboard writer; `push_plain_notice` is
  `pushNotice(text, 'plain')`.

## Notes for the lead

* `tests/goldens/pickers-extensions.json` is checked by `node tests/recorders/record-pickers-extensions.mjs --tree <checkout>
  --check tests/goldens/pickers-extensions.json`. It was recorded on `D:/mixdog-build/mig/ref/node` (the copy of the Node tree at
  the same commit), with inert stand-ins for the packages that tree has no `node_modules` for. 33 scenarios; the Rust test
  `tests/pickers_extensions.rs` replays them over a scripted store and compares every channel (store calls, notices, painted
  panels, prompt changes, openers, clipboard, hints) per step.
* The late "Not used" ack of the Agents picker named for this task in `nr-tui-surface-layout.wire` belongs to
  `route-pickers/agents-picker.mjs` (nr-tui-pickers-model), not to a file this task owns; the "Esc during a pending Plugins open"
  case and the late plugin-write ack are tests here (`a_list_that_lands_after_esc_is_not_painted`,
  `a_plugin_write_that_acks_after_esc_does_not_reopen_the_list`).
